# TinyRoute requirements

Source of truth (do not duplicate; read when implementing or designing):

- `docs/requirements/Functional.md`
- `docs/requirements/Non-Functional.md`

## Scope guardrails

- Portfolio URL shortener for one developer; keep it small and deployable.
- Redirects are public (no account). Create/manage requires a signed-in account.
- Prefer Must over Should over Could. Prefer MVP over V1 over Future.
- Do not implement out-of-MVP work unless the user explicitly asks: custom aliases, expiration, analytics, public API, password reset, blocklist, social login, admin console.

## MVP (build this)

Accounts (email/password), authenticated HTTPS-only link creation, unique codes, public redirect with correct unknown/disabled/deleted handling, owner-only list/disable/re-enable/delete, rate limits on create and auth (redirect throttle Should).

## Key NFRs (MVP)

- Redirect p95 under 150 ms, p99 under 300 ms server-side at ~100 rps sustained
- Create/list/manage p95 under 500 ms
- Fail closed: never guess a destination when state is unknown
- Health check endpoint; single-region, modest hardware

## When in doubt

Open or `@`-mention the requirements docs before adding features, changing behavior, or inventing APIs/architecture that conflict with them.
